\begin{lemma}[Smooth annular uniformization]\label{lem:annular-uniformization}
\uses{thm:rf-harmonic-radius}
\lean{PoincareMT.M64Uniformization.exists_smooth_annular_cover_chart}
A smooth positive metric on the planar annulus admits a harmonic
function with boundary values zero and one, a conjugate on its
universal cover, and a positive flux period. Their normalized pair
is a smooth coordinate diffeomorphism onto a strip, equivariant
under the deck translation.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Solve the scalar Dirichlet problem. Local harmonic coordinates and
the maximum principle control its level sets; the boundary flux is
positive. The conjugate closed one-form integrates on the cover.
Its period and the noncritical harmonic coordinate give a proper
one-to-one map to the normalized strip. The inverse function theorem
upgrades the inverse to smoothness.
\end{proof}

